# Elixir Koans - 11 Sigils

```elixir
import ExUnit.Assertions
```

## The ~s sigil is a different way of expressing string literals

```elixir
assert ~s{This is a string} == ___
```

## Sigils are useful to avoid escaping quotes in strings

```elixir
assert "\"Welcome to the jungle\", they said." == ___
```

## Sigils can use different delimiters

```elixir
matches? = ~s{This works!} == ~s[This works!]
assert matches? == ___
```

## The lowercase ~s sigil supports string interpolation

```elixir
assert ~s[1 + 1 = #{1 + 1}] == ___
```

## The ~S sigil is similar to ~s but doesn't do interpolation

```elixir
assert ~S[1 + 1 = #{1+1}] == ___
```

## The ~w sigil creates word lists

```elixir
assert ~w(Hello world) == ___
```

## The ~w sigil also allows interpolation

```elixir
assert ~w(Hello 1#{1 + 1}3) == ___
```

## The ~W sigil behaves to ~w as ~S behaves to ~s

```elixir
assert ~W(Hello #{1+1}) == ___
```

